@startuml
' Question: What is the ordered sequence of messages between participants
' to satisfy <subject>? Use this when timing, ordering, async, returns,
' or notes matter more than static structure.
'
' Audience: <delivery teams, integration architects, review board>
'
' Replace placeholder participant names and message labels. Keep the
' "Related Artifacts" comment block at the bottom up to date.

title <Subject> sequence

actor "<Actor / Stakeholder>" as Actor
participant "<Application 1>" as App1
participant "<Application Service>" as Svc
participant "<Technology Component\n(e.g. queue, DB)>" as Tech
participant "<External Application>" as Ext

Actor -> App1 : <user action>
App1 -> Svc : <method or message>(<correlation_id>)
Svc -> Tech : <persist / publish>
Tech --> Svc : <ack>
Svc -> Ext : <forward / call>
Ext --> Svc : <response>
Svc --> App1 : <result>
App1 --> Actor : <feedback>

note over Svc,Tech
    Capture invariants here:
    - correlation_id propagated end-to-end
    - retry / replay policy
    - timeout / circuit-breaker stance
end note

' Related Artifacts:
' - APP-XXXX (each participant)
' - AS-XXXX (application services)
' - IF-XXXX (each cross-application call)
' - TC-XXXX (technology components used)
' - STK-XXXX (the human actor at the top)
@enduml
